e: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the retirement/cleanup lifecycle (or explicit boundedness rationale) for the per-MCP-identity session logs the pointer now rotates across, so they do not accumulate unboundedly on the long-running server.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the server-side session-log pointer rotates per MCP identity instead of one shared log, accepted and documented' — states the create/update but names no retirement path","Every distinct hint value under a principal produces a new session-log pointer; hints derive from client-supplied per-session ids (e.g. ${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID}), so the identity space grows with every agent session on a long-lived server","T9(d): shared state with no defined retirement path leaks/accumulates"],"finding":"The plan changes the server-side session-log pointer to rotate per MCP identity ('mcp:<principal>' or 'mcp:<principal>/<hint>') instead of one shared log, but never states a RETIRE/cleanup path for the resulting proliferation of per-identity session logs — with a distinct log created for every principal and every hint value, these accumulate unboundedly on the long-running server.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0505bb95fa90a556","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Resolver consumers: 'session_log.py:58/151/184 — the server-side session-log pointer rotates per MCP identity instead of one shared log, accepted and documented'","norm_id":"n0f45c55fcd1039bd","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A long-running MCP server serving many agent sessions accumulates one session log per unique principal/hint pair, with no bound or cleanup, growing without limit across deployments"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the docs/event-schema.md note on the session-log pointer effect, state either a cleanup/rotation bound or why the per-identity log count is inherently bounded (e.g. reused across reconnects) so it does not leak.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the composite-verifier citation from `src/rebar/mcp_server.py:615` (the stdio else-branch, which has no HTTP surface) to the HTTP branch at lines ~587-594 where `FastMCP(... token_verifier=... , streamable_http_path=...)` actually installs `AuthContextMiddleware` over the Streamable-HTTP app.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.0062,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["mcp_server.py:612-615 is the `else:` stdio branch: `mcp = FastMCP(\"rebar\", token_verifier=token_verifier, auth=auth_settings)` with comment 'stdio has no HTTP surface — ... the SDK only enforces auth over HTTP'","mcp_server.py:587-594 is the HTTP branch: `FastMCP(\"rebar\", host=host, port=port, streamable_http_path=path, ..., token_verifier=token_verifier, auth=auth_settings, stateless_http=True)` — this is where streamable_http_app()/AuthContextMiddleware apply","The composite verifier is passed on both branches, so the underlying premise (SDK carries the accepted principal per HTTP request) holds; only the citation is mislocated"],"finding":"The Approach cites 'rebar passes its composite at src/rebar/mcp_server.py:615' as the point where FastMCP.streamable_http_app() installs AuthContextMiddleware, but line 615 is the stdio else-branch whose own comment states 'stdio has no HTTP surface — ... the SDK only enforces auth over HTTP.' The HTTP path that actually constructs the streamable app with the verifier is lines 587-594. The principal seam depends on AuthContextMiddleware running over HTTP; the cited line is the one branch where it does not.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8260a43c61c983c8","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Principal seam bullet ('rebar passes its composite at src/rebar/mcp_server.py:615')","norm_id":"n2a81a0f8bc5b29e6","priority":0.7438,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader/implementer follows the cited line to wire or verify the AuthContextMiddleware seam and lands on the stdio branch where the middleware never runs"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Replace the citation with the HTTP construction site (mcp_server.py:587-594), or cite both branches while noting AuthContextMiddleware is installed only on the HTTP branch.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State in the Approach (and update the session_id.py precedence docstring) why the MCP identity source is placed ABOVE REBAR_SESSION_ID — i.e. per-request MCP identity must outrank the server process's own env — and confirm this intentionally supersedes the documented 'authoritative override' semantics for the MCP path.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4763,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'resolve_session_id() gains one higher-precedence source ahead of REBAR_SESSION_ID'","session_id.py:10-12: 'the explicit, rebar-owned REBAR_SESSION_ID (an operator/hook override is authoritative)'","The MCP-ahead placement is correct for the goal (client identity must beat the server's own env) but inverts the documented authoritative-override invariant without